NAME
     head - the first part of a file

SYNOPSIS
     head [-n LINES] [-c BYTES] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     head copies the first ten lines of each FILE, or of standard input.
     With more than one FILE it puts a header before each.

OPTIONS
     -n LINES   how many lines
     -c BYTES   that many bytes instead of lines

SEE ALSO
     tail(1), cat(1)
